{
    "name": "Peterson Goodwyn",
    "birthDate": "1745",
    "deathDate": "1818-02-21",
    "bio": "a Representative from Virginia; born at \"Martins,\" near Petersburg, Dinwiddie County, Va., in 1745; received his education from private tutors; completed preparatory studies; engaged in planting; studied law; admitted to the bar in 1776 and commenced practice in Petersburg, Va., and surrounding counties; served in the Revolutionary War, equipped his own company, and rose from captain to major; promoted to colonel for gallantry at the battles of Smithfield and Great Bridge; member, Virginia state house of delegates, 1789-1802; elected as a Democratic Republican to the Eighth and to the seven succeeding Congresses and served from March 4, 1803, until his death at his home, \"Sweden,\" in Dinwiddie County, Va., February 21, 1818; interment in the family burying ground on his estate.",
